---
alwaysApply: true
---

1. Commit changes following proper workflow
   1.1. Always ask for permission before committing changes
   1.2. Split commits by logical subjects - one commit per completed feature/fix
   1.3. Use single-line commit messages with clear, descriptive subject lines
   1.4. Show proposed commit message and files to be committed
2. Push commits regularly to the current branch
   2.1. Push after each completed feature/fix commit
   2.2. Push before switching branches or ending work session
   2.3. Push to keep remote repository synchronized
